From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:33:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll iOS: sync and timer census counters, ECO QoS switch,
 processor-count override

- PE side: contended critical-section census (count, wait-time histogram,
  sampled ring of contended locks), WaitOnAddress wake counts, and a
  per-thread QueryPerformanceCounter gap histogram, exported as ios_xp_nt for
  the probe.
- Unix side: counters for SetEvent/ResetEvent/PulseEvent, single and multiple
  waits (zero-timeout polls counted separately), yields and delays by
  requested duration.
- ECO: madeira_set_eco() moves every guest thread to a low QoS class
  (madeira.cfg eco-qos, default utility); each thread applies the change on
  its next wait, sleep or yield, since QoS can only be set on self.
- madeira.cfg cpu-count = N reports N processors to Windows code (experiment).

